WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.200
- Welcome back y'all.

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.810
We are very lucky to have
one of the greats with us,

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:05.051
Miss Dionne Warwick.

00:00:05.051 --> 00:00:07.339
(audience applauds)

00:00:07.339 --> 00:00:08.910
Our next guest is a talented musician

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:11.280
and an Oscar nominated
record producer who's worked

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:14.670
with artists like Macy
Gray, Pink, and Beyonce.

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:15.989
Never heard him, I'm just kidding.

00:00:15.989 --> 00:00:19.170
He also happens to be Dionne's son.

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.180
Together they have a new single out now.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:22.350
It's called I Kneel

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:24.090
and they'll be releasing
an album next year

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.410
called Songs of Inspiration.

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:27.349
Please welcome Damon Elliot, everybody.

00:00:27.349 --> 00:00:29.049
(audience applauds)

00:00:29.049 --> 00:00:31.716
(upbeat music)

00:00:50.229 --> 00:00:51.270
Man, Dionne's your Mom.

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:52.103
Let's just start with that.

00:00:52.103 --> 00:00:52.936
That's crazy.

00:00:52.936 --> 00:00:54.030
- That's pretty cool.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:54.942
- Yeah.

00:00:54.942 --> 00:00:57.360
What did you think? How old
were you when she scolded

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.040
Snoop Dogg and Suge Night?

00:00:59.040 --> 00:00:59.940
- Oh, are we going to that story?

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:00.773
Okay, yeah.

00:01:00.773 --> 00:01:02.010
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:03.180
- I'm still reliving that.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:04.731
- I know, like where, what year?

00:01:04.731 --> 00:01:07.319
- I think I was around seven 18.

00:01:07.319 --> 00:01:08.182
Maybe 19.

00:01:08.182 --> 00:01:09.015
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:01:09.015 --> 00:01:11.233
- Right around the Declaration
of Independence time.

00:01:11.233 --> 00:01:12.120
(audience applauds)

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:13.410
Throwing me under the bus Ma.

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:15.462
We the people, that's...

00:01:15.462 --> 00:01:16.890
- That's how it starts.

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:18.600
Do you, were you ever, were you the kid

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:19.560
that like snuck out at all?

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:20.702
Did you ever get busted?

00:01:20.702 --> 00:01:21.590
- Did I ever?

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:22.423
- Oh man.

00:01:22.423 --> 00:01:25.620
- Did I ever, that's why I
got sent to military school.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:27.020
- Oh, you went to military school?

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:27.853
- I did, I did.

00:01:27.853 --> 00:01:28.686
- You really needed to
be straightened out.

00:01:28.686 --> 00:01:31.920
Okay, okay, okay. okay.

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:33.289
No, but that's awesome though.

00:01:33.289 --> 00:01:36.021
And in the sense of like,
just growing up around,

00:01:36.021 --> 00:01:38.070
I don't know, just growing
up in the industry so much.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:39.990
I often wonder about my kids like,

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:41.340
'cause they're always around people

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:42.390
and they think it's so normal.

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:44.340
Like, and then you obviously
gravitated towards the

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:45.840
same line of work.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:46.673
- Sure.

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:47.506
- [Kelly] Was it always in
the cards for you like that?

00:01:47.506 --> 00:01:48.339
Did you always...

00:01:48.339 --> 00:01:50.280
- I knew from like day one

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:53.040
or at least maybe day six years in,

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:54.076
seven years into my life.

00:01:54.076 --> 00:01:54.930
- Yeah.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:58.048
- Not day one, but that
I wanted to be in music

00:01:58.048 --> 00:02:01.920
and I never wanted to be a
firefighter or a police officer.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:02.880
I always wanted to do music.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:07.170
I drove my mom absolutely
crazy singing all in the house.

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:09.030
Maybe not being the best
singer in the family,

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:09.863
just being honest.

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:10.696
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:10.696 --> 00:02:11.590
- So I turned into a producer.

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:12.423
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:12.423 --> 00:02:13.280
- And it worked out okay.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:14.340
- [Kelly] It worked out real well.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:16.230
- Thank God.

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:17.550
- I'd say so, yeah.

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:18.780
I mean, even the names listed,

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:20.340
those are incredible names
that you've been able

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.450
to like work with over the career

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:23.130
and now you're doing something together.

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:23.963
- Yes.

00:02:23.963 --> 00:02:24.796
- Who thought of this?

00:02:24.796 --> 00:02:27.090
Who thought of the idea
to do the gospel album?

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:27.923
- Me.

00:02:27.923 --> 00:02:28.756
- [Kelly] You did?

00:02:28.756 --> 00:02:29.613
- Yeah, I did.

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:35.570
I feel what we're going
through now, universally.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:36.473
- [Kelly] People need it.

00:02:36.473 --> 00:02:39.300
- We need some words of
inspiration and of courage.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:41.180
(audience applauds)

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:42.731
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:42.731 --> 00:02:47.731
- You know, coming from
a gospel singing family,

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:52.593
you know, understanding that gospel is

00:02:52.593 --> 00:02:56.190
actually the Bible in song.

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:57.930
And that those that,

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:01.523
well maybe we're getting
too far away from the Bible

00:03:01.523 --> 00:03:03.810
and what it really means.

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:06.720
So let's put some of that
back into people's ears

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:07.830
and hearts.

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:08.663
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:08.663 --> 00:03:09.496
(audience applauds)

00:03:09.496 --> 00:03:10.329
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:03:10.329 --> 00:03:13.260
So what was the inspiration for I Kneel?

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:14.093
That's the song, right?

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:17.420
- So I kneel is a really,
really personal song

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:19.200
to both Mom and myself.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:23.142
When I co-wrote the
song with Greg and Jared

00:03:23.142 --> 00:03:26.070
and the guys, it actually was inspired

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:28.320
by a young lady who's here today.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:29.610
Her name is Alexis Silva.

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:32.970
And she went through
this bout at 15 years old

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:34.830
well she was 14 at the time.

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:39.120
And it was amazing to see how
Mom turned to God in prayer.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:42.321
And I remember she said
specifically to Alexis's father,

00:03:42.321 --> 00:03:43.650
God's got this.

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:45.660
And we just absolutely, we prayed

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:47.190
and we prayed and we prayed.

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:50.438
And ironically the same time
when the song was coming out,

00:03:50.438 --> 00:03:54.600
she beat what it was that
she was going through.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.910
And it just shows the testament.

00:03:56.910 --> 00:04:00.120
It just shows that how,
when you really believe

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:03.300
and you really get down
on your knees and pray

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:04.170
God will answer.

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:05.003
- [Kelly] And God's timing.

00:04:05.003 --> 00:04:05.947
- [Dionne[ It's powerful.

00:04:05.947 --> 00:04:06.780
- [Kelly] Yeah, it's powerful.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:07.613
- Yeah.

00:04:07.613 --> 00:04:08.446
- Yeah.

00:04:08.446 --> 00:04:09.600
And the timing of that is incredible.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:10.590
How do you dismiss that?

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:11.423
You know what I'm saying?

00:04:11.423 --> 00:04:12.420
Like how does that...

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:13.253
- You don't.

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:14.086
- Yeah, don't dismiss it.

00:04:14.086 --> 00:04:14.919
Yeah, no, absolutely, absolutely.

00:04:14.919 --> 00:04:17.070
So what's it like to see,

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:18.570
I mean, you had to be a little nervous

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:19.920
with him going into the business.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:21.270
It can be a very hard business.

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:23.550
So watching your kid get
involved in that, like what is

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:25.080
that like to see him succeed?

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:26.040
- It's wonderful.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:27.780
You know, it's like I told him, I said,

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:30.718
if you're going to do it, make
sure you're the best at it.

00:04:30.718 --> 00:04:31.551
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:31.551 --> 00:04:32.850
- You have to hone your craft.

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:33.683
- Yeah.

00:04:33.683 --> 00:04:34.516
- It's not given to you.

00:04:34.516 --> 00:04:35.617
You will earn it.

00:04:35.617 --> 00:04:37.980
And that's exactly what he did.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:39.555
- Driving her crazy every day.

00:04:39.555 --> 00:04:43.410
Playing her demo after demo after demo.

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:44.243
Woo.

00:04:44.243 --> 00:04:45.330
- Look, I apologized to my mom too.

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:46.350
I sang so much.

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:48.870
We had lived in a tiny
duplex, so yeah, yeah.

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:49.740
Or an apartment.

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:51.265
So she was like, shut up.

00:04:51.265 --> 00:04:52.650
(audience laughs)

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:54.210
And I'm out there like, singing Ariel

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:55.260
part of your world or something.

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:56.854
Like I was, I never shut up.

00:04:56.854 --> 00:04:58.526
But it worked out Mom.

00:04:58.526 --> 00:05:00.300
- She does this thing with her head

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.010
where if you're not hitting
the right notes, she's like,

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:03.167
kinda like (makes screeching noise)

00:05:03.167 --> 00:05:08.167
so I probably gave you some
neck problems quite a few times.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:11.393
- My mom would not nod her
head, she'd just be like, no.

00:05:11.393 --> 00:05:12.600
(all laugh)

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.752
She'd be like, she's very truthful.

00:05:14.752 --> 00:05:16.410
But it's working out now.

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:17.730
It's working out for both of us now.

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:18.570
- Yes, indeed.

00:05:18.570 --> 00:05:19.403
- So if you have a kid

00:05:19.403 --> 00:05:21.240
that's driving you crazy in
your home, it's gonna be fine.

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:22.170
- [Damon] It's gonna be fine.

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:23.700
- We have to take another break.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:26.310
You can listen to Dionne
and Damon's single I Kneel,

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:27.570
wherever you get your music,

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:28.860
and look for their album as well.

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:30.600
It's called Songs of Inspiration.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:32.000
Next year that's coming out.

